<title>ESTONIA: HUVITUSFOND 9TH SERIES OVERSUBSCRIBED.</title>
<headline>HUVITUSFOND 9TH SERIES OVERSUBSCRIBED.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Huvitusfond's ninth bond issue was oversubscribed 1.6 times, the compensation voucher fund company said on Friday.</p>
<p>In a statement, the fund said the total volume of the issue was 30 million kroons and they received purchase orders worth 50 million kroons.</p>
<p>The biggest buyers of the bonds were banks of which Hansapank bought the most, the fund said.</p>
<p>The ninth series bonds have a five-year maturity and interest is paid every three months based on the Talibor plus 1.5 percent.</p>
<p>The fund trades in bonds based on compensation vouchers which were given to residents in compensation for unreturned property or for years worked.</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 620 9201/2 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
